resume: Postcolonial thinking is a radical critical epistemology, founded on the colonial civilizing mission as matrix and legacy. Behind postcolonial criticism lies a great rationalist narrative issued by the Enlightenment — a unilateral, linear vision of history. In spite of its universalist pretentions, the Enlightenment tends to be a way of perceiving the world through a Western lens.
